ev":17558.7,"fmp_official_ev":17558.7,"enterpriseValueBasis":"USD market capitalization + USD debt - USD cash and short-term investments","dcf_model_ev":5456.9,"ev_to_ebitda":28,"debt_to_ebitda":0.23,"net_debt_to_ebitda":-2.13,"f_score":8,"f_score_breakdown":[{"id":1,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率 ROA > 0","passed":1,"detail":"當期 ROA = 7.7%"},{"id":2,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"營業現金流 CFO > 0","passed":1,"detail":"自由現金流 = $305M"},{"id":3,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率持續擴張 (ΔROA > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":1,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 18.6%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 4.91"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":59.87,"default_fair_val":59.87,"premium_pct":178.1,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":65.3,"pe_forward":57.5,"pb_trailing":6.1,"pb_forward":5.5,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":15.5,"fcf_to_ev":1.73,"fcf_to_mcap":1.61,"liab_to_assets":18.6,"cash_to_assets":39.3,"current_ratio":4.91,"roe":9.4,"roa":7.7,"moat":{"ticker":"TSEM","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"TSEM 在半導體製造領域，品牌和定價權相對較弱。其業務模式為晶圓代工，主要客戶為無廠半導體公司，這意味著 TSEM 的議價能力受客戶需求和市場競爭的影響較大。與龍頭廠商如台積電相比，TSEM 在品牌知名度和技術領先性上存在差距，難以形成顯著的定價優勢。其產品屬於技術密集型，但並非獨特或高附加價值的品牌商品，因此在品牌定價權方面得分不高。","comment_en":"TSEM has relatively weak brand and pricing power in the semiconductor manufacturing sector. Its business model as a foundry means its primary customers are fabless semiconductor companies, making TSEM's bargaining power significantly influenced by customer demand and market competition. Compared to industry leaders like TSMC, TSEM lags in brand recognition and technological leadership, making it difficult to establish a distinct pricing advantage. While its products are technology-intensive, they are not unique or high-value-added branded goods, thus scoring low on brand pricing power."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"TSEM 作為一家成熟的晶圓代工廠，擁有一定的製程技術和專利組合，這構成了其進入壁壘。然而，半導體產業的專利競爭激烈且更新換代快，TSEM 的專利壁壘相較於專注於特定高階技術或擁有關鍵IP的公司（如ASML的光刻技術）而言，並非絕對的壟斷性優勢。其專利主要集中在成熟製程和特定應用領域，監管方面則面臨全球半導體產業的複雜地緣政治和貿易限制，這既是挑戰也是一種保護，但非絕對的特許經營權。","comment_en":"As a mature foundry, TSEM possesses a certain level of process technology and patent portfolio, which forms its entry barrier. However, patent competition in the semiconductor industry is fierce and rapidly evolving. TSEM's patent barrier is not an absolute monopolistic advantage compared to companies focused on specific high-end technologies or possessing critical IP (like ASML's lithography technology). Its patents are mainly concentrated in mature processes and specific application areas. In terms of regulation, it faces complex geopolitical and trade restrictions in the global semiconductor industry, which acts as both a challenge and a form of protection, but not an absolute franchise."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"對於使用 TSEM 晶圓代工服務的客戶而言，更換供應商的轉換成本相對較高。這主要體現在重新設計、驗證和測試新製程的巨大時間和金錢投入。客戶與 TSEM 建立的長期合作關係，以及對其特定製程能力的依賴，都增加了轉換的難度。尤其是在成熟製程領域，客戶的產品設計往往與特定代工廠的製程緊密綁定，因此 TSEM 在此方面具有一定的客戶黏性。","comment_en":"For customers utilizing TSEM's foundry services, the switching costs to change suppliers are relatively high. This is primarily reflected in the significant time and financial investment required for redesign, re-validation, and re-testing with new processes. The long-term cooperative relationships customers have established with TSEM, and their reliance on its specific process capabilities, increase the difficulty of switching. Especially in mature process areas, customer product designs are often tightly coupled with a specific foundry's processes, thus TSEM possesses a certain degree of customer stickiness in this regard."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"TSEM 的業務模式（晶圓代工）本質上不具備顯著的網絡效應。其價值主要來自於生產能力、技術和成本效率，而非用戶數量增加帶來的邊際效益遞增。與社交媒體或市場平台不同，TSEM 的客戶關係是點對點的，一個客戶的增加並不會直接提升其他客戶的價值或吸引力。因此，在網絡效應這一維度上，TSEM 的護城河非常薄弱。","comment_en":"TSEM's business model (foundry) inherently lacks significant network effects. Its value primarily derives from production capacity, technology, and cost efficiency, rather than increasing marginal benefits from a growing user base. Unlike social media or marketplace platforms, TSEM's customer relationships are point-to-point; the addition of one customer does not directly enhance the value or attractiveness for other customers. Therefore, TSEM's moat in terms of network effects is very weak."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"TSEM 作為一家成熟的晶圓代工廠，透過其規模化的生產設施和營運經驗，能夠在成熟製程領域實現一定的成本優勢。規模經濟有助於降低單位生產成本，使其在與其他代工廠的價格競爭中佔據有利地位。然而，相較於全球最大的晶圓代工廠，TSEM 的規模優勢並非絕對領先，尤其是在最先進製程方面。但對於其專注的利基市場，規模帶來的成本效益仍然是重要的競爭壁壘。","comment_en":"As a mature foundry, TSEM leverages its scaled production facilities and operational experience to achieve certain cost advantages in mature process segments. Economies of scale help reduce unit production costs, positioning it favorably in price competition with other foundries. However, compared to the world's largest foundries, TSEM's scale advantage is not absolutely leading, especially in the most advanced processes. Nevertheless, for the niche markets it focuses on, the cost efficiencies derived from scale remain an important competitive barrier."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"TSEM 在地理位置上擁有其生產基地，例如在以色列、美國和歐洲，這有助於服務當地客戶並分散地緣政治風險。然而，這些地理資產並非獨一無二或不可複製的。半導體製造業的關鍵在於技術和人才，而非單純的地理位置。雖然在地緣政治考量下，區域性生產基地有其戰略價值，但這並不能構成 TSEM 獨有的、強大的經濟護城河。","comment_en":"TSEM has production bases in various geographies, such as Israel, the US, and Europe, which helps serve local customers and diversify geopolitical risks. However, these geographical assets are neither unique nor irreplicable. The key to the semiconductor manufacturing industry lies in technology and talent, not merely location. While regional production bases hold strategic value amid geopolitical considerations, this does not constitute a unique and strong economic moat for TSEM."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"TSEM 在成熟製程的營運效率方面表現穩健。其長期積累的製程知識和生產管理經驗，使其能夠在成本控制和產品質量之間取得良好平衡。穩定的 F-Score (8/9) 和健康的自由現金流 (FCF TTM: $304.6M) 以及較低的負債比率，都顯示了其良好的營運管理能力。這種效率是建立在多年經驗和持續優化之上的，構成了其在特定市場區隔中的競爭優勢。","comment_en":"TSEM demonstrates solid operational efficiency in mature process technologies. Its long-accumulated process knowledge and production management experience enable a good balance between cost control and product quality. A stable F-Score (8/9), healthy Free Cash Flow (FCF TTM: $304.6M), and a low debt ratio all indicate strong operational management capabilities. This efficiency is built upon years of experience and continuous optimization, forming its competitive advantage within specific market segments."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"TSEM 的財務狀況顯示其擁有充裕的現金儲備（$1,481.4M）和較低的負債（$141.7M），這為其資本配置提供了靈活性。公司需要將資本有效地分配於研發、擴產、併購或股東回報。雖然 TSEM 的 ROE (9.4%) 和 ROA (7.7%) 顯示其盈利能力尚可，但與頂尖半導體公司相比仍有提升空間。其過往的資本配置決策，特別是併購策略，對其長期價值有重要影響，但其效率有待進一步觀察。","comment_en":"TSEM's financial position shows ample cash reserves ($1,481.4M) and low debt ($141.7M), providing flexibility for capital allocation. The company needs to effectively allocate capital towards R&D, capacity expansion, M&A, or shareholder returns. While TSEM's ROE (9.4%) and ROA (7.7%) indicate decent profitability, there is room for improvement compared to top semiconductor companies. Its past capital allocation decisions, particularly M&A strategies, significantly impact its long-term value, but their efficiency warrants further observation."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"如 M3 所述，TSEM 在其服務的客戶群中具有較高的客戶留存率。這得益於晶圓代工業務的轉換成本，以及 TSEM 在特定成熟製程領域的穩定性和可靠性。客戶一旦選擇了 TSEM 並投入了相應的設計和驗證，通常會傾向於維持長期合作關係，以確保生產的連續性和成本效益。這種客戶黏性是 TSEM 穩定營收的重要保障。","comment_en":"As mentioned in M3, TSEM enjoys a high customer retention rate among its client base. This is attributed to the switching costs inherent in the foundry business and TSEM's stability and reliability in specific mature process technologies. Once customers choose TSEM and invest in corresponding design and validation, they tend to maintain long-term cooperative relationships to ensure production continuity and cost-effectiveness. This customer stickiness is a crucial guarantee for TSEM's stable revenue."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"TSEM 的護城河耐久性取決於其在成熟製程領域的持續競爭力以及應對技術變革的能力。雖然成熟製程需求穩定，但長期來看，半導體產業的技術迭代和新興應用（如 AI、高效能運算）對傳統代工廠構成挑戰。TSEM 需要不斷投資於製程優化和產能擴張，以維持其成本優勢和客戶關係。其耐久性相對穩固，但並非像某些擁有獨特專利或強大品牌影響力的公司那樣具有長遠的抗顛覆性。","comment_en":"The durability of TSEM's moat depends on its sustained competitiveness in mature process technologies and its ability to adapt to technological changes. While demand for mature processes is stable, the industry's technological evolution and emerging applications (like AI, high-performance computing) pose challenges to traditional foundries in the long run. TSEM needs continuous investment in process optimization and capacity expansion to maintain its cost advantages and customer relationships. Its durability is relatively stable but lacks the long-term anti-disruption potential of companies with unique patents or strong brand influence."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Tower Semiconductor (TSEM) 在半導體代工領域，其護城河主要體現在成熟製程的轉換成本（M3）和營運效率（M7）上，這為其帶來了相對穩定的客戶關係（M9）和一定的成本優勢（M5）。然而，其品牌定價權（M1）和網絡效應（M4）較弱，專利壁壘（M2）和地理資產（M6）亦非絕對領先。整體而言，TSEM 屬於一個具有特定利基市場優勢的「收費橋」類型公司，其護城河相對穩固但並非無懈可擊，耐久性（M10）受產業技術快速變革的影響。管理層的資本配置（M8）效率將是未來擴大優勢的關鍵。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Tower Semiconductor (TSEM) operates in the semiconductor foundry space, with its moat primarily stemming from switching costs in mature processes (M3) and operational efficiency (M7), which foster relatively stable customer relationships (M9) and certain cost advantages (M5). However, its brand pricing power (M1) and network effects (M4) are weak, and its patent barriers (M2) and geographical assets (M6) are not absolutely leading. Overall, TSEM can be characterized as a 'toll bridge' type company with advantages in specific niche markets. Its moat is relatively solid but not impregnable, and its durability (M10) is influenced by the rapid technological changes in the industry. Management's capital allocation efficiency (M8) will be key to expanding its advantages in the future.","evidenceHash":"fd40474485f5ca2552fdd734f63ca1ee1c31a5df5c301f81c18e6b8735e54fd1","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T05:19:36.013Z","evidenceHash":"760e586af78ef2e8084a0c8072252ad4b52f523fcc50d47b0ae2145a65a3386d"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T05:19:36.013Z","evidenceHash":"760e586af78ef2e8084a0c8072252ad4b52f523fcc50d47b0ae2145a65a3386d"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TSEM.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TSEM.png","website":"https://towersemi.com","ceo":"Russell C. Ellwanger","full_time_employees":"5613","description":"Tower Semiconductor Ltd. operates as a prominent independent semiconductor foundry, engaged in the worldwide production and sale of analog-intensive, mixed-signal semiconductor components. The company provides a comprehensive suite of customizable process technologies, including SiGe, BiCMOS, mixed signal/CMOS, RF CMOS, CMOS image sensors, integrated power management solutions, and MEMS. Furthermore, it offers wafer fabrication services, a design enablement platform to streamline the development process, and specialized services for process transfer optimization and new product development. Tower Semiconductor caters to both integrated device manufacturers and fabless companies, with its products serving a wide range of industries such as consumer electronics, computing, telecommunications, automotive, industrial, aerospace, defense, and medical devices. Established in 1993 and based in Migdal Haemek, Israel, its market reach extends across the United States, Japan, other Asian regions, and Europe.","description_en":"Tower Semiconductor Ltd. operates as a prominent independent semiconductor foundry, engaged in the worldwide production and sale of analog-intensive, mixed-signal semiconductor components. The company provides a comprehensive suite of customizable process technologies, including SiGe, BiCMOS, mixed signal/CMOS, RF CMOS, CMOS image sensors, integrated power management solutions, and MEMS. Furthermore, it offers wafer fabrication services, a design enablement platform to streamline the development process, and specialized services for process transfer optimization and new product development. Tower Semiconductor caters to both integrated device manufacturers and fabless companies, with its products serving a wide range of industries such as consumer electronics, computing, telecommunications, automotive, industrial, aerospace, defense, and medical devices. Established in 1993 and based in Migdal Haemek, Israel, its market reach extends across the United States, Japan, other Asian regions, and Europe.","description_zh":"**Tower Semiconductor Ltd. (TSEM) 業務營運概述**\n\nTower Semiconductor Ltd. 是一家領先的獨立半導體晶圓代工廠，專注於全球製造與銷售類比訊號密集型、混合訊號半導體元件。公司提供一系列客製化的製程技術，涵蓋矽鍺 (SiGe)、雙極互補金屬氧化物半導體 (BiCMOS)、混合訊號/CMOS、射頻 (RF) CMOS、CMOS 影像感測器、整合式電源管理解決方案，以及微機電系統 (MEMS)。\n\n此外，Tower Semiconductor 提供晶圓代工服務、簡化開發流程的設計賦能平台，以及製程轉移優化與新產品開發的專業服務。其客戶群涵蓋整合元件製造商 (IDM) 與無廠半導體公司 (Fabless)，產品廣泛應用於消費性電子、運算、通訊、汽車、工業、航太、國防及醫療設備等多元產業。公司成立於 1993 年，總部位於以色列，業務遍及美國、日本、亞洲其他地區及歐洲。","address":"Ramat Gavriel Industrial Park","city":"Migdal Haemek","state":"HZ","zip":"2310502","country":"IL","phone":"972 4 650 6611","full_address":"Ramat Gavriel Industrial Park, Migdal Haemek, HZ 2310502, IL","range_52w":"80.63-319.94","year_high":319.94,"year_low":80.63,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":80.63,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Chelouche Yoav","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":232,"price":215.06,"total_val":0.05},{"date":"2026-08-12","name":"Ellwanger Russell Craig","title":"officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":1025,"price":245.93,"total_val":0.25},{"date":"2026-08-12","name":"Ellwanger Russell Craig","title":"officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":2062,"price":246.71,"total_val":0.51},{"date":"2026-08-12","name":"Ellwanger Russell Craig","title":"officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":5498,"price":248.02,"total_val":1.36},{"date":"2026-08-12","name":"Ellwanger Russell Craig","title":"officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":5559,"price":248.94,"total_val":1.38},{"date":"2026-08-12","name":"Ellwanger Russell Craig","title":"officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":1123,"price":250.05,"total_val":0.28},{"date":"2026-08-12","name":"Ellwanger Russell Craig","title":"officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":6474,"price":251.04,"total_val":1.63},{"date":"2026-08-12","name":"Ellwanger Russell Craig","title":"officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":3341,"price":252.07,"total_val":0.84},{"date":"2026-08-12","name":"